{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dear Marie,\n\nI am in Dresden this evening. The air here is heavy and warm, but I have recovered. Early tomorrow morning I was in the Picture Gallery and looked at the new exhibition. People speak a lot about Romanticism, but I stick to my judgment: Art must represent the True as a whole, not just moods or individual sensibilities. The works that pleased me were those in which the individual subordinated itself to the universal.\n\nAfter that, I went to the Brühl Terrace. The view of the Elbe is magnificent, and one feels free there, as if standing above everyday worries. I conversed with Mr. Ammon for an hour. He is a witty man, and we spoke about the development of the spirit in art history. It is good to have such conversations, for the loneliness of travel becomes more bearable through exchange with other minds.\n\nI am now going back to the Gallery to check a few more details, and then I will visit Tieck. He is here and will surely tell me a lot about the literary trends in Vienna.\n\nGreetings to the boys. Kiss.\n\nYour G. W. F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795221171,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":240,"prompt_tokens":340,"total_tokens":580,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-MmOuNCNCVuuXzvgWKzzbT0qr1lKc6G8n","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":340,"prompt_ms":468.022,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.376535294117647,"prompt_per_second":726.4615765925533,"predicted_n":240,"predicted_ms":5652.634,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.651188284518827,"predicted_per_second":42.28117369707644}}